The recommended way to write Git commit messages is to use imperative mood, keep the subject short, and describe what the commit changes.
Standard format
<type>: <short description>


Common types:
Type	When to use	Example
feat	Add a new feature	feat: add refresh token ID to auth API
fix	Fix a bug	fix: resolve refresh token validation issue
refactor	Improve code without changing behavior	refactor: simplify token generation logic
test	Add or update tests	test: add refresh token validation tests
docs	Update documentation	docs: update authentication API documentation
chore	Maintenance or configuration	chore: update Maven dependencies